=   entry .Error   raised when a resource is not on the classpath
-     detail
+     detail

-         Error `↯/s.67.1`: _the resource `path` was not on the classpath_. Raised by the `Streamable`
-         givens for `Resource` and `Path on Classpath` when the `Classloader` in scope does
-         not have the resource. A `cp"…"` resource is checked at compile time against the
-         compiler's classpath, so this error at runtime means the program was launched with a
-         different one.
-     entry #resource   the path which was asked for
-   entry .Event   what a classloader logs as it reads resources
+         Error `↯/s.67.1`: _the resource `path` was not on the classpath_. Lo lanzan los givens
+         `Streamable` para `Resource` y `Path on Classpath` cuando el `Classloader` del ámbito
+         no tiene el recurso. Un recurso `cp"…"` se comprueba en tiempo de compilación contra
+         el classpath del compilador, así que este error en tiempo de ejecución significa que
+         el programa se lanzó con uno distinto.
+     entry #resource   la ruta que se pidió
+   entry .Event   lo que registra un cargador de clases mientras lee recursos

=   entry .Event   what a classloader logs as it reads resources
-     detail
+     detail

-         Every `Event` is tagged `Log.Runtime` and `Log.Resource`, so a logging configuration
-         can select or silence them by tag. `Classloader#apply` logs `ResourceLoaded` at
-         `fine`, and a failed read logs `ResourceMissing` as a warning before raising
-         `Classpath.Error`. A `Classpath.Event is Loggable` must be in scope for the logged
-         reads; `logging.silentLogging` discards them.
-     entry .communicable   renders each event as a message
-     entry .ResourceLoaded   a resource was read: _loaded the classpath resource `path`_
-       entry #path   the resource's path
-     entry .ResourceMissing   a resource was not found: _the classpath resource `path` was not found_
-       entry #path   the resource's path
-   entry #entries   the classpath's entries, in search order
+         Todo `Event` lleva las etiquetas `Log.Runtime` y `Log.Resource`, de modo que una
+         configuración de registro puede seleccionarlos o silenciarlos por etiqueta.
+         `Classloader#apply` registra `ResourceLoaded` en `fine`, y una lectura fallida
+         registra `ResourceMissing` como advertencia antes de lanzar `Classpath.Error`. Para
+         las lecturas registradas debe haber un `Classpath.Event is Loggable` en el ámbito;
+         `logging.silentLogging` los descarta.
+     entry .communicable   representa cada evento como un mensaje
+     entry .ResourceLoaded   se leyó un recurso: _loaded the classpath resource `path`_
+       entry #path   la ruta del recurso
+     entry .ResourceMissing   no se encontró un recurso: _the classpath resource `path` was not found_
+       entry #path   la ruta del recurso
+   entry #entries   las entradas del classpath, en orden de búsqueda

